      "extract": "In this section we introduce spherical Hopf algebras. These are defined to be Hopf algebras with some additional structure which implies that the category of finitely generated modules is a spherical category. Definition 3.1. A spherical Hopf algebra over F consists of F-module A together with the following data (1) a multiplication + (2) a unit ': F \u0014 A (3) a comultiplication 2: A \u0014A\u0017A (4) a counit =: A \u0014 F (5) an",
